Scope
-----

The licence covers the *derived datasets* (the normalised JSON in `data/`): the
selection, normalisation, de-duplication, part-of-speech tagging and
provenance metadata added by this project. It does not transfer any rights in
the upstream files themselves, which remain the property of their respective
copyright holders and are never redistributed by this project. The corpus index
in `data/corpus.json` publishes metadata only.

The band descriptors in `src/data/bands.ts` are original condensed paraphrases
written for this project. They are not the official IELTS band descriptors,
which are published by the British Council, IDP: IELTS Australia and Cambridge
Assessment English (https://www.ielts.org/for-organisations/ielts-scoring-in-detail).
Researchers who need the authoritative wording must cite the published
descriptors directly.

The score concordances in `src/data/conversions.ts` are indicative values
compiled from the test providers' own published comparison tables. Receiving
institutions apply their own rules; always verify against the current published
table.

The source code of this project is licensed separately under the MIT licence —
see LICENSE.

Reading/Listening extension
---------------------------

The compilation in data/practice.json contains only selected Git tree metadata.
Its original schema, selection and annotations are CC BY 4.0. The indexed source,
https://github.com/ngoclong1209/UPGRADE-YOUR-IELTS-SKILLS, had no identified content
licence at commit ba7a0f2bf13be89c601bab2f9e72d1007f49bb2c. Each response preserves
that unknown upstream licence as null. Exercise text, answer keys, audio,
documents, upstream code and learner data are NOT included. Our metadata licence
does not license or authorise redistribution of any indexed upstream file.

The independently written task-family guidance in src/data/receptive-tasks.ts is
also CC BY 4.0. It is not official IELTS wording, an official marking rubric, or
a promise of a particular score. Authoritative format references accompany the
guidance.

For the legacy vocabulary dataset, the provenance and rights of dictionary-style
glosses remain unresolved (see RESEARCH.md). Attribution and format conversion do
not themselves clear third-party rights. Do not interpret this licence as a
blanket permission for upstream content.
